---
import { MoveRight } from '@lucide/astro';
---

<section class="adaptive-reading-overview not-prose" aria-labelledby="adaptive-reading-overview-title">
  <p class="overview-kicker">Overview · ~2 min</p>
  <h2 id="adaptive-reading-overview-title">The interface knows the state. The guidance knows the why.</h2>
  <p class="overview-lead">
    A user configuring a Data Connection may need an explanation scattered across documentation or release notes. This research asks what happens when the application selects applicable authored knowledge at that point of need—without letting documentation, or a future AI layer, decide product truth.
  </p>

  <figure class="overview-orientation" aria-labelledby="adaptive-orientation-title">
    <div class="orientation-heading">
      <h3 id="adaptive-orientation-title">Move the knowledge. Keep the authority.</h3>
      <p class="figure-label">At the Data Connection field</p>
    </div>

    <div class="orientation-grid">
      <section class="knowledge-side">
        <p class="figure-label figure-accent">Moves into the task</p>
        <h4>Applicable guidance</h4>
        <p>Authored explanations selected for this version, familiarity, and field state.</p>
        <MoveRight size={20} strokeWidth={1.5} aria-hidden="true" />
      </section>

      <section class="authority-side">
        <p class="figure-label">Stays with the application</p>
        <h4>Truth &amp; permission to act</h4>
        <p>Current selection, compatible options, required-field validation, and the response boundary.</p>
        <p class="authority-rule">A relevant note cannot choose a value.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <figcaption>
      An orientation to the proposed separation, not a live decision trace. The companion project owns the working interaction; the research explains its boundaries.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="overview-section" aria-labelledby="adaptive-short-method">
    <h3 id="adaptive-short-method">Adaptation without inference</h3>
    <p>
      Phase 1 compares standard and adaptive forms under the same scenario, application state, and required-field validation. The adaptive form selects small authored fixtures using explicit conditions such as version, simulated familiarity, and field state. No LLM or remote inference is needed. Whether a fragment <em>applies</em> is one question; whether the interface may explain, guide, or offer a value is a separate policy decision.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="overview-section overview-separated" aria-labelledby="adaptive-short-evidence">
    <h3 id="adaptive-short-evidence">Evidence sets the ceiling</h3>
    <p>
      With several compatible connections, the user’s intent is unresolved: explain the requirement or guide attention, but do not guess. With exactly one compatible connection, the interface may offer “Use connection”; the user must accept it. Familiarity and version can change the explanation, not validity. Once a valid selection exists, missing-field intervention ends.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="overview-section overview-separated" aria-labelledby="adaptive-short-open">
    <h3 id="adaptive-short-open">A reference experiment, not an outcome claim</h3>
    <p>
      The scenarios are fixed, the knowledge is authored fixture data, and familiarity is simulated. There is no document ingestion, semantic retrieval, behavioral learning, or measured UX improvement here. Governance of stale or conflicting guidance remains open. Later inference might map intent or rank candidates <em>after</em> deterministic filtering, but its output would still be checked against application truth and response policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="overview-continue">
    <p>Continue into the seven concerns, decision path, scenario evidence, limitations, and the optional AI seam.</p>
    <button type="button" data-reading-depth-open="full">
      Full Research · ~8 min <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </button>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .adaptive-reading-overview {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .adaptive-reading-overview :global(h2),
  .adaptive-reading-overview :global(h3),
  .adaptive-reading-overview :global(h4),
  .adaptive-reading-overview :global(p),
  .adaptive-reading-overview :global(figure),
  .adaptive-reading-overview :global(figcaption) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .overview-kicker,
  .figure-label {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-mono-ui);
    font-size: var(--research-figure-label, 0.625rem) !important;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    line-height: 1.5 !important;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .overview-kicker,
  .figure-accent {
    color: var(--accent) !important;
  }

  .adaptive-reading-overview > h2 {
    margin-top: 0.7rem !important;
    max-width: 42rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.65rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .overview-lead {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-top: 1.1rem !important;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 1rem !important;
    line-height: 1.8 !important;
  }

  .overview-orientation {
    margin-top: 2.5rem !important;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-block: 1.75rem;
  }

  .orientation-heading {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem;
  }

  .orientation-heading h3 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .orientation-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .orientation-grid section {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .knowledge-side {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }

  .knowledge-side h4,
  .authority-side h4 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem !important;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .knowledge-side h4 + p,
  .authority-side h4 + p {
    margin-top: 0.5rem !important;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--research-figure-copy, 0.875rem) !important;
    line-height: 1.65 !important;
  }

  .knowledge-side :global(svg) {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .authority-side {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .authority-rule {
    margin-top: 1rem !important;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: var(--research-figure-support, 0.75rem) !important;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.6 !important;
  }

  .overview-orientation figcaption {
    margin-top: 1.75rem !important;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--research-figure-caption, 0.75rem) !important;
    line-height: 1.65 !important;
  }

  .overview-section {
    max-width: 46rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  .overview-section h3 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  }

  .overview-section p {
    margin-top: 0.8rem !important;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.95rem !important;
    line-height: 1.8 !important;
  }

  .overview-section em {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .overview-separated {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-top: 2rem;
  }

  .overview-continue {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem 2rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .overview-continue > p {
    max-width: 24rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem !important;
    line-height: 1.65 !important;
  }

  .overview-continue button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.5;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .overview-continue button:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
  }

  .overview-continue button:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .overview-orientation {
      padding-block: 2.25rem;
    }

    .orientation-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 2rem;
    }

    .knowledge-side {
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
    }

    .authority-side {
      margin-top: 0;
      border-top: 0;
      border-left: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
      padding: 0 0 0 1.75rem;
    }

    .knowledge-side :global(svg),
    .authority-rule {
      margin-top: 1.25rem !important;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .overview-continue button {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
